.TH QUADRF-LOAD 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-load \- program the FPGA and bring up the QuadRF radio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-load
.RB [ \-\-detect | \-\-bist ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unloads
.BR fpga_csi ,
detects the ECP5 variant (LFE5U-45F or LFE5U-25F) over JTAG with OpenOCD,
programs the matching
.I /usr/share/quadrf/fpga/quadrf-45.svf
or
.I /usr/share/quadrf/fpga/quadrf-25.svf
bitstream, loads the
.B fpga-dsi
and
.B fpga-csi
drivers against the new bitstream and finishes with
.BR "quadrf-jtag \-\-init"
(and
.B bist
when invoked with
.B \-\-bist
or through
.BR load-quadrf.service ).
.PP
.B load-quadrf.service
runs this at boot. It is safe to run again by hand, which is the quickest way
to recover a board that has lost its bitstream.
.PP
The OpenOCD binary comes from
.B QUADRF_OPENOCD
if that is set, otherwise from
.I /usr/lib/quadrf/openocd/bin/openocd
or
.IR /usr/bin/openocd .
Stock OpenOCD cannot drive JTAG on a Pi 5; install
.B quadrf-openocd
for a build with RP1 GPIO support.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/quadrf/fpga/quadrf.svf
Bitstream.
.TP
.I /usr/share/quadrf/openocd/board/rpi5_lfe5u45f.cfg
OpenOCD board configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR quadrf.conf (5)
